&lt;p&gt;Join the team turning internet intelligence into real-world security outcomes. Built on the world’s most comprehensive and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;cen016-po-underline&quot; href=&quot;https://censys.com/internet-map/&quot;&gt;accurate map of the Internet&lt;/a&gt;, the Censys Platform delivers real-time visibility and actionable intelligence needed to accelerate triage, investigate threats, hunt adversaries, and manage Internet exposure. We&#39;re trusted by half of the Fortune 500 and government agencies all around the world, and looking for people as passionate about the problems we&#39;re solving as we are.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Censys has emerged as a leader in internet-scale attack surface management — and we&#39;re scaling the sales org to match. This is your shot to own the Pacific Northwest at exactly the moment a Series D, category-defining security company needs its next great territory builder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report to our Area VP of Sales (West) and sit alongside a sharp bench of Sales Engineers, Channel Managers, and SDRs who move fast and back each other up. You won&#39;t just be closing deals in one of the most security-sophisticated regions in the country — Seattle and Portland&#39;s density of enterprise cloud, SaaS, and security buyers makes this one of the highest-leverage territories in the company. You&#39;ll also help write the playbook other AEs use as we scale, working directly with sales leadership to shape process, not just execute it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re energized by category-leader momentum but still want the freedom (and occasional chaos) of building something from a still-early stage — territory strategy, deal structure, even parts of the sales motion aren&#39;t fully fixed yet — this is built for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
