&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team turning internet intelligence into real-world security outcomes. Built on the world’s most comprehensive and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;cen016-po-underline&quot; href=&quot;https://censys.com/internet-map/&quot;&gt;accurate map of the Internet&lt;/a&gt;, the Censys Platform delivers real-time visibility and actionable intelligence needed to accelerate triage, investigate threats, hunt adversaries, and manage Internet exposure. We&#39;re trusted by half of the Fortune 500 and government agencies all around the world, and looking for people as passionate about the problems we&#39;re solving as we are.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Integrations Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to help build and evolve our next-generation Censys Platform. You’ll work closely with product and engineering teams building, deploying and maintaining scalable integrations between our Censys platform and third-party systems such as SIEMs, SOARs, and Threat Intelligence Platforms (TIPs). These integrations connect Censys Platform with critical security platforms, enriching attack surface data and delivering actionable insights directly into the tools practitioners and CISOs depend on for visibility, threat hunting and incident response. You will play a critical part in helping organizations and critical security providers of all shapes and sizes truly understand everything on the Internet and help make it a safer place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical direction for Censys&#39;s integrations portfolio: decide what we build and how we build it, across a dozen-plus integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead integration delivery across internal engineers and external vendor partners, setting standards, reviewing work, and ensuring long-term maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain integrations with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP) and security operations platforms (SIEM, SOAR, TIP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with third-party engineering teams, and with our Alliances and Marketing teams, to launch and certify integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and maintain robust integrations between the Censys Platform and external SOAR, SIEM, and TIP solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and operate highly available, scalable API connectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and maintain existing Censys open-source APIs and SDKs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance the next generation of integrations by developing AI Agent skills and plugins to support Agentic workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create instructions for AI Agents to build new integrations and maintain existing ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement automated solutions for continuous integration, covering the building, testing, monitoring, and deployment of integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strong advocate for the customer, prioritizing requests, and actively shaping the integrations roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep current with emerging SOAR, SIEM, and TIP technologies to inform and guide the overall integration strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own it! Independently drive and implement integrations, working closely with PM, customer success, and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical leadership: you&#39;ve set direction for a multi-integration or platform effort and grown the engineers around you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in software engineering, with at least 3+ years focused on integrations and robust backend systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python, Go, or Java Experience (3+ years)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;API: Deep expertise in API-first development and seamless service integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master Integrator: Proven ability to unify multiple APIs into a coherent platform with solid service contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD Champion: Always pushing to improve deployment and developer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code Craftsmanship: Passionate about writing clean, maintainable, and scalable code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Action-Oriented: Bias for action and an iterative approach to solving problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-Driven Thinker: Contribute insightful ideas to technical discussions, making fast, informed decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication Powerhouse: Excellent communication and documentation skills — able to clearly explain technical concepts across engineering and non-engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Sets You Apart:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience integrating with security platforms (e.g., Splunk, Cortex XSOAR, Anomali, Recorded Future).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A cyber security engineering background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success integrating with vendor marketplaces (e.g., AWS, Splunk)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with expanding REST/gRPC micro-service architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in harnessing AI and LLM&amp;nbsp; tools as a force multiplier - using it to code smarter, iterate faster boosting productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud providers, (especially Google Cloud)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in building, deploying, and maintaining containerized services in Kubernetes environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand the value of building maintainable software, while building new services you are ensuring test coverage is enforced by strong CI practices, adding linters and code complexity checks. You value clean abstraction, and promote established design patterns, but also know when to innovate beyond conventions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Job level and actual compensation will be decided based on factors including, but not limited to, individual qualifications objectively assessed during the interview process (including skills and prior relevant experience, potential impact, and scope of role), market demands, and specific work location. The listed range is a guideline, and the range for this role may be modified. For roles that are available to be filled remotely, the pay range is localized according to employee work location by a factor of between 83% and 100% of range. Please discuss your specific work location with your recruiter for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will work to ensure individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to apply for a role, participate in the interview process, perform essential job functions, and receive other benefits and privileges of employment. If you require accommodation, please reach out to your recruiter. These modifications enable an individual with a disability to have an equal opportunity not only to get a job, but successfully perform their job tasks to the same extent as people without disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To ensure the integrity of our hiring process and in attempt to facilitate a more personal connection, we require all candidates to keep their cameras on during video interviews. You may also be required to meet a Censys employee at one point during your process. Additionally, if hired, you will be invited to visit Ann Arbor, Michigan for in-person onboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By applying for this job, the candidate acknowledges and agrees that any personal data contained in their application or supporting materials will be processed in accordance with our &lt;a href=&quot;https://censys.com/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;Censys Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
